{{smaller block|Without the officiousness, the inquisitiveness, the effrontery, the ''toad-eating,'' the insensibility to all reproof, he [Boswell] never could have produced so excellent a book.
{{right|''Macaulay'', Boswell's Johnson.}}}}

'''toad-eating''' (tōd′ē″ting), ''a.'' Pertaining to or characteristic of a toad-eater or sycophant; sycophantic.

